import json,html
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(__file__).parent
r=json.loads((root/'results.json').read_text())
variants=['current_paidPunch','energyOnly_paidPunch','current_freePunch','energyOnly_freePunch']
labels=['Checked defense + paid Punch','Guaranteed defense + paid Punch','Checked defense + free Punch','Guaranteed defense + free Punch']
names={'attack':'Punch whenever possible','prepareEveryOther':'Alternate Prepare / Punch','prepareOnTell':'Prepare on rat tell','defendOnTell':'Defend on rat tell','defendWhenHurt':'Prepare/Punch; defend on tell if HP≤4 and Energy≥3','bankDefense':'Bank defense with Energy≥3; otherwise Prepare/Punch','random':'Uniform random legal action'}
pct=lambda v:f'{100*v:.2f}%'
body='''<html><body style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif;max-width:1100px;margin:32px auto;line-height:1.5"><h1>Rat combat balance: defense checks and Punch cost</h1><p>2 November 2026. Frozen snapshot of rat-alternative.json. Rat 4 HP; player 10 HP; Agility 3; initial Energy 3. A separate sensitivity run starts at 10 Energy.</p><p><b>Rules compared:</b> checked defense uses the engine’s 3d6 ≥ 10 reaction roll (62.5% block chance after a hit); guaranteed defense blocks the hit without a defense roll, still costs 1 Energy and uses the same action/guard timing. Rat defense and attack dice are unchanged. Paid Punch costs 1 Energy; free Punch costs 0. Punch deals 1–2 base damage; free Prepare adds 2 and breaks a rat block (the preparation bonus is absorbed by breaking the block).</p>'''
body+='<p><b>Main finding at the current 3 Energy start:</b> repeated Punch rises from 24.70% wins to 89.05% when Punch is free. Defend-on-tell with free Punch rises from 87.47% with checked defense to 94.34% with guaranteed defense. The best observed paid-Punch strategy wins 74.95% under either defense rule. Recommendation: try free Punch plus guaranteed paid defense if the goal is reliable, understandable defense; expect a forgiving first encounter and retune rat difficulty separately if that is too easy.</p>'
for s in r['scenarios']:
 body+=f'<h2>Starting Energy {s["energy"]}</h2><table border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="6"><tr><th>Strategy</th>'+''.join(f'<th>{l}</th>' for l in labels)+'</tr>'
 for k,label in names.items():
  body+='<tr><td>'+label+'</td>'+''.join('<td>'+pct(s['variants'][v][k]['winRate'])+'</td>' for v in variants)+'</tr>'
 body+='</table><h3>Best observed strategy in this sample (not a proof of optimal play)</h3><table border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="6"><tr><th>Variant</th><th>Strategy</th><th>Win rate (95% Wilson interval)</th><th>Winner HP</th><th>Winner Energy</th><th>Mean choices, all fights</th></tr>'
 for v,l in zip(variants,labels):
  k,d=max(s['variants'][v].items(),key=lambda item:item[1]['winRate'])
  body+=f'<tr><td>{l}</td><td>{names[k]}</td><td>{pct(d["winRate"])} ({pct(d["confidence95"][0])}–{pct(d["confidence95"][1])})</td><td>{d["winnerHp"]:.2f}</td><td>{d["winnerEnergy"]:.2f}</td><td>{d["meanDecisions"]:.2f}</td></tr>'
 body+='</table>'
body+='''<h2>How to read this</h2><p>Defense competes directly with Punch for the starting Energy budget. Guaranteed defense improves protection when chosen, but cannot by itself repair a strategy that spends the Energy needed to kill the rat. Free Punch removes that failure mode and makes defense spending less punishing. Preparing remains a strong offensive option. These are strategy-specific encounter outcomes, not a measurement of campaign balance or proof that one strategy is optimal.</p><h2>Method and verification</h2><p>10,000 seeded headless production-coordinator encounters per cell; 7 strategies × 4 variants × 2 Energy starts = 560,000 retained encounters. An independent code review caught and corrected the random policy so it selects uniformly from legal actions, including free Punch at zero Energy. No-defense policy results are asserted identical across the defense variants. Unaffordable actions fall back to the free Prepare action until the encounter resolves; there is no Energy regeneration. Player choices see HP, rat HP, Energy, preparation, guard and the visible rat preparation cue; they never see its hidden block/charge branch. Shared seeds reproduce each cell but removing rolls changes later random-number alignment, so comparisons are not paired identical trajectories. Win intervals describe sampling uncertainty, not model uncertainty. Winner HP and Energy are conditional on victory.</p><p>37 relevant existing engine tests passed. Physical dice, browser presentation, animation and devices were not tested. The original project and production engine were not edited. The guaranteed-defense variant exists only as an isolated analysis override.</p><p>Snapshot SHA-256: '''+r['sourceSha256']+'</p></body></html>'
(root/'report.html').write_text(body)
print('Saved report.html')
